---
// Shared drawn-line icon sprite (direction §2.1 grammar, closing.md "ten
// glyphs (shared sprite)"). Referenced via <use> by Receipts.astro (the
// icon marquee) and Footer.astro (the 12px credit-line mark) — the only
// two consumers.
//
// LOAD-BEARING CONSTRAINT: every symbol holds exactly ONE <path> (multiple
// `M` moveto commands for disconnected sub-strokes, arc-pairs for the two
// circular glyphs). A <use> element cannot expose per-child
// stroke-dasharray, so a glyph built from several independent
// path/line/circle primitives could not be draw-in animated as one unit
// through a single <use> reference — collapsing to one path per symbol
// means stroke-dasharray/stroke-dashoffset set on the <use> itself (or on
// the real <path> below, for length-measurement) correctly drives the
// whole glyph's draw-in. Do not "simplify" a glyph back into multiple
// elements without also rebuilding the draw-in mechanism. `d` strings are
// verbatim from specs-v2/closing.md.
//
// The wrapper is visually hidden via the "position:absolute; 0x0;
// overflow:hidden" technique rather than `display:none` — `display:none`
// removes an SVG subtree from the render tree in Chromium, which makes
// `getTotalLength()` on the real <path> (how Receipts.astro measures each
// glyph for its draw-in) return 0. This keeps the sprite invisible while
// staying measurable.
---

<svg
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
  class="tf-glyph-sprite"
  style="position:absolute; width:0; height:0; overflow:hidden;"
>
